# ── Vendored skill tree (skills/) ───────────────────────────────────────────
# Everything under skills/ is vendored upstream CONTENT, and scripts/lib/hash.mjs
# hashes every file it finds there into the lockfile (snapshotHash/contentHash).
# A file that git ignores but the hash covers would make the committed tree fail
# to reproduce its own lock entry, so the generic build-output, log and dotenv
# rules above must never win inside skills/. These files are already public in
# their upstream repositories, so re-including them exposes nothing new.
#
# `.env` is re-included as an EXPLICIT, tested policy: an upstream `.env` that
# is public in its own repository is vendored content like any other file, and
# scripts/test/gitignore-scope.test.mjs (GI1/GI6) pins that it is both tracked
# and hashed. This exception is scoped to skills/**; the repository's own `.env`
# above stays ignored.
#
# node_modules/ is deliberately NOT re-included: a dependency tree is never
# legitimate vendored content and re-including it would risk committing
# thousands of files. Because it can never be tracked, it is also excluded from
# staging and from the hash (scripts/lib/hash.mjs HASH_EXCLUDED_DIRECTORIES), so
# neither side ever claims provenance for bytes the other cannot see.
!/skills/**/bin/
!/skills/**/obj/
!/skills/**/dist/
!/skills/**/build/
!/skills/**/output/
!/skills/**/*.log
!/skills/**/.env
